### 1.3 Asset Dependency Graph — 235 Edges

Built with **NetworkX** directed graph:
- Edge A → B means "A depends on B"
- If B fails, everything depending on B transitively is affected

**Realistic dependency layers:**
```
STORAGE (SAN-01)
  └→ DATABASES (DB-MAIN-01, DB-STUDENT-01, ...)
      └→ SERVICES (SVC-AUTH-01, SVC-CACHE-01, ...)
          └→ APIs (API-STUDENT-01, API-EXAM-01, ...)
              └→ APPLICATIONS (APP-PORTAL-01, APP-ERP-01, ...)
                  └→ USER DEVICES (Workstations)
```

**Graph capabilities:**
- `get_blast_radius(asset_id)` — how many assets would fail if this one dies
- `find_cascading_path(source, target)` — how failure propagates between two assets
- `find_critical_assets(top_n)` — most impactful assets by betweenness centrality + dependents + criticality
- `get_single_points_of_failure()` — nodes whose removal disconnects the graph

