## 🟨 PART 2 — AI INTELLIGENCE ENGINE (📋 DESIGNED, PENDING BUILD)

### Agent Pipeline

```
EVENT STREAM → SENTINEL → INVESTIGATOR → EVIDENCE AGENT → DEPENDENCY AGENT →
SECURITY AGENT → ROOT CAUSE ENGINE → PLANNER → COUNTERFACTUAL ENGINE →
RISK ENGINE → EXECUTOR → VERIFIER → RECOVERY/REPLANNING
```

### Agent Descriptions

| # | Agent | Purpose | Input | Output |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Sentinel** | Continuous monitoring | Events, metrics, incidents, state | NORMAL / WARNING / ANOMALY / CRITICAL |
| 2 | **Investigator** | Collect evidence, generate hypotheses | Recent events, logs, metrics, history, config changes, dependencies | Multiple hypotheses with confidence |
| 3 | **Evidence Agent** | Evidence-based reasoning layer | Claims, raw data | Evidence items with supporting/contradicting data + confidence |
| 4 | **Dependency Agent** | Graph traversal + blast radius | Asset ID, dependency graph | Affected services, upstream/downstream, blast radius, criticality |
| 5 | **Security Agent** | Classify incidents | Events, patterns | OPERATIONAL_FAILURE / CONFIGURATION_ERROR / HUMAN_ERROR / SECURITY_EVENT / UNKNOWN |
| 6 | **Root Cause Engine** | Combine all analysis | Evidence, dependencies, history, metrics, security classification | Root cause + confidence + affected systems + evidence |
| 7 | **Planner** | Generate multiple remediation plans | Root cause, affected systems, memory | Multiple plans with actions, risk, downtime, rollback method |
| 8 | **Counterfactual Engine** | "What if" simulation | Candidate plans | Expected recovery %, risk %, downtime, secondary failures |
| 9 | **Risk Engine** | 0-100 risk scoring | Proposed actions | Risk score determining auto-execute / supervisor / human / block |
| 10 | **Executor** | Execute permitted tools | Selected plan | Tool execution results |
| 11 | **Verifier** | Measure + compare | Before/after metrics | SUCCESS / FAILED |
| 12 | **Recovery** | Rollback + replan | Failed verification | Rollback → new plan → re-execute |

### Risk Levels

| Score | Level | Action |
|---|---|---|
| 0–30 | LOW | Auto execute |
| 31–60 | MEDIUM | Supervisor review |
| 61–80 | HIGH | Human approval required |
| 81–100 | CRITICAL | Blocked |

